Main Characteristics of Marconi's RadiH and Epoch
Eight planets on the east side of the natal chart signify Marconi's tireless efforts to develop his inventions, especially his remarkable extension of radio waves up to the short-wave band.
His ingenuity is shown by the trine of MERCURY, semisextile MC (orb 20'), to URANUS, with JUPITER semisquare URANUS.
VENUS and PLUTO also apply their creative trines to JUPITER, while VENUS in the 11th house, two degrees from the trine, secured Marconi a host of supporters. However PLUTO, whose mundane position falls in the 12th house by nine degrees, caused much litigation, mainly over infringement of his patents.
His lack of speaking and lecturing skills is indicated by SATURN opposition cusp 3, to 14' of arc ( 17' in mundo).
The MOON applies by sextile to ASC and JUPITER, broadcasting his success worldwide.
His heart trouble which eventually caused his death at the age of 63 is mainly characterised by the midpoint combination: ASC = SUN/URANUS (orb 23').

The prenatal epoch again shows an extrovert personality, with seven planets on the east side of the chart reinforcing the radix with an angular JUPITER on the IC.
VENUS elevated improves his personal and private life. SUN closely opposing SATURN may have caused some shyness when addressing audiences. It may have hindered his sex life too.

These examples show that a serious and thorough delineation of both radix and epoch. free of fictional notions and false judgements, only becomes possible if the horoscope is rectified to within seconds of time. In addition. the prenatal epoch frequently exhibits more features of the native's character and destiny than the radix.

